# Per-stage overrides for SWARM_ENV=staging. Copy to `env/staging.env` (gitignored
# — see .gitignore) and fill in the real values; `scripts/compose` requires that
# file to exist for SWARM_ENV=staging (ADR-0015).
#
# `staging` is today's ONE live internal instance (ADR-14: real data, internal
# users, fast iteration — see docs/STATE.md). Its single-GPU consilium fleet
# (small, GPU-resident models instead of the heavy decorrelated default panel)
# and `GROUP_SCOPE_MAP` already have sensible fallbacks directly in
# `docker-compose.yml` (`SWARM_CONSILIUM_PANEL`, `SWARM_CONSILIUM_JUDGE`) —
# nothing to duplicate here. This file is where a future per-corpus calibration
# knob (e.g. `SWARM_ENRICH_THRESHOLD`, `SWARM_ER_VEC_THRESHOLD` — currently set
# ad hoc only for the manually-run cognitive-loop script, never the always-on
# kernel) would land if and when the operator decides to wire it into the
# deployed kernel, not before — that is a product-behavior decision, not a
# config-mechanism one, and stays out of scope here (ADR-0015).

# --- web_channel / Keycloak public hostnames (hive-publish-readiness-audit) ---
# NOT secrets — but REQUIRED (no compose default) because there is no safe generic
# value: the OIDC issuer must be a hostname both the browser AND the web_channel
# container can resolve to the SAME thing (the "dev split-horizon" trick — see
# docker-compose.yml). Intranet-specific, so this whole FILE (not these three keys
# alone) is gitignored rather than committed. Set all three to the same real host
# (e.g. this machine's real hostname/IP on the network you access it from) + the
# published ports:
KEYCLOAK_PUBLIC_URL=
WEB_CHANNEL_PUBLIC_URL=
KEYCLOAK_PUBLIC_HOST=

# --- Postgres (kernel substrate) ---
